I wrote the session plan for Day 248 (21:32), but it isn't committed. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the commit was refused. I left it that way rather than forcing it with git add -f, since the instruction's || true already allows for the commit not happening. The files are at session_plan/task_01.md, task_02.md and issue_responses.md.

Task 1: Part of #1064 (product, my own pick). MCP servers that yoyo starts as child processes currently inherit every provider API key. @yuanhao decided they should get those keys removed by default, the way hooks already do, and yoagent 0.26.8 (already in the lock file) now has the function that does it.
• The change: one helper in src/mcp_prefix.rs builds the start options for both places these servers are launched, so it's one edit. It reuses the hooks' existing on/off rule and key list. YOYO_SUBPROCESS_ENV_SCRUB=0 or false turns the removal off, and a misspelled value keeps it on.
• The cost: a server that quietly relied on an inherited key will now fail its own calls. It can still be given a key explicitly through [mcp_servers.<name>] env, and the docs and commit will say so.
• The test: a new test runs the real yoyo binary with a stub server that just writes its environment to a file. It checks the key is missing, that an ordinary variable still gets through, and that each setting of the env var does what it should. The task also has the implementer break the fix on purpose, watch the test fail, then restore it.
• Left open on #1064: the opt-in wiring for /run, !, /bg and /watch, bash inside sub-agents, and the goal_verify command.

Task 2: Fixes #1130 (product, the backlog-drain slot). yoyo review -- --quick should treat --quick as a file name, but it's still read as the effort flag, because the review path joins the arguments into one string and splits them again. The task keeps the effort flag and the target as separate values, reads flags only before --, and leaves the REPL's /review alone. Since it removes that join-and-split step, the test table gets a separate row for each input it used to treat the same: empty arguments, a path with a space, and the --pr5 form.

Two issues filed while planning:
• #1131: yoyo thinks ast-grep is installed whenever any sg command runs. On this runner sg is an unrelated system command, so yoyo ast fails with a confusing error and yoyo map falsely reports it is "using ast-grep".
• #1132: ast, blame and test still treat an unknown --word as an argument instead of refusing it, as the seven verbs fixed under #1111 now do. #1111 was closed, so these three had no issue tracking them.

Deferred: #1126 and #1128 sit in the prompt area, which already took 5 of the last 10 self-driven changes, and prompt_retry.rs is at its size limit. No release: the cadence says one isn't due.
